cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this course or its measured baselines, please cite it as below."
title: "nanodrone-ai: a sim-first, on-device autonomy course for 27 g micro-drones"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Hans"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-07-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/csinghans/nanodrone-ai"
url: "https://csinghans.github.io/nanodrone-ai/"
abstract: >-
  A bilingual (English / Traditional Chinese) 30-lesson open-source course
  that teaches on-device AI autonomy for nano-drones: from a first simulated
  hover to a nano V-JEPA-style latent world model that anticipates collisions
  before they happen, under a 512 KB int8 on-board budget. Every lesson ships
  a selftest that prints and asserts its own measured result.
keywords:
  - drones
  - world-models
  - embedded-ai
  - reinforcement-learning
  - education
